{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevL61gdkWJ2N6No1ygjd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Now let me summarize the analysis findings and move to the design phase.\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nImplement a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions orders to CANCELLED status, cancels associated CREATED shipments, with idempotent behavior for already-cancelled orders, all-or-nothing rejection if any shipment is CONFIRMED, 404 for non-existent orders, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt): currently has no status field\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:15): has POST create and GET endpoints  \n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10): in-memory ConcurrentHashMap store\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9): has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:26): no order validation on shipment creation\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10): no findByOrderId method\n- Exception handling (ApiExceptions.kt:19-24): ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException patterns established\n- Error codes (ApiError.kt:31): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions this repository uses:**\n1. Exceptions thrown in controllers caught by GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16)\n2. Status codes: 201 CREATED for POST, 200 OK for successful responses, 409 CONFLICT for state violations, 404 NOT_FOUND for missing resources\n3. Error responses structured as `{error: {code, message, fields}}` (ApiError.kt:16)\n4. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on both status and error body (OrderControllerTest.kt:59-74)\n5. Data classes are immutable with fields passed at construction\n\n**Affected files (why each cannot be avoided):**\n1. Order.kt - must add status field to represent order state\n2. OrderController.kt - must add cancel endpoint (POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel)\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - must add findByOrderId to locate shipments needing cancellation\n4. ShipmentController.kt - must validate order status exists and is not CANCELLED before creating shipment\n5. ApiError.kt - must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code for shipment rejection case\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - must test all cancel cases (success, already cancelled, confirmed shipment blocks, unknown order)\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - must test shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Adding status field to Order changes the data contract - existing order creation must default to ACTIVE\n2. All-or-nothing semantics requires checking all shipments before modifying any state\n3. Race conditions in in-memory store (ConcurrentHashMap protects writes but not multi-step operations)\n4. Idempotent cancellation of already-cancelled orders must not throw error\n\n**Open questions:** None - the requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field (non-nullable, defaults to ACTIVE). Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed; save method already handles updates to existing orders.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** - Add `cancel(@PathVariable orderId: String): ResponseEntity<Order>` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, returns 200 with the order (idempotent)\n   - Checks all shipments for this orderId\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code without modifying anything\n   - Otherwise, cancels all CREATED shipments and updates order to CANCELLED, returns 200 with updated order\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify create method to:\n   - After checking shipment doesn't exist, check that the order exists (ResourceNotFoundException if not)\n   - Check that the order is not CANCELLED (ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED if it is)\n   - Then proceed with shipment creation\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum for shipment rejection case.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order succeeds with 200 and order is CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling CREATED shipments are transitioned to CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an already-CANCELLED order succeeds with 200 (idempotent)\n   - Cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and nothing changes\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order fails with 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n1. **OrderStatus as separate enum file**: Rejected - keep it in Order.kt following ShipmentStatus pattern (Shipment.kt:23)\n\n2. **Soft delete (mark deleted)**: Rejected - requirement says CANCELLED is a distinct status used in business logic, not a delete\n\n3. **ServiceLayer for order cancellation**: Rejected - not needed; controller can orchestrate repository calls directly given the in-memory store simplicity and lack of transaction boundaries\n\n4. **Check order existence in ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId**: Rejected - let ShipmentRepository just find shipments; ShipmentController validates order exists separately\n\n5. **Add OrderRepository.findShipmentsForOrder**: Rejected - ShipmentRepository is the owner of Shipment data; add method there instead\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments):**\n  - Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n  - OrderController reads order (found, ACTIVE)\n  - OrderController reads all shipments for O-1 (finds S-1 in CREATED, S-2 in CREATED)\n  - Checks no CONFIRMED shipments (passes)\n  - Updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED in ShipmentRepository\n  - Updates order to CANCELLED in OrderRepository\n  - Response: 200 with Order(status=CANCELLED)\n\n- **Already cancelled (idempotent):**\n  - Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel (order already CANCELLED)\n  - OrderController reads order (found, CANCELLED)\n  - OrderController reads all shipments\n  - Checks no CONFIRMED shipments\n  - No shipments to update\n  - Updates order to CANCELLED (no-op since already CANCELLED)\n  - Response: 200 with Order(status=CANCELLED)\n\n- **Blocked by CONFIRMED shipment (all-or-nothing):**\n  - Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel (order ACTIVE, has S-1 CONFIRMED)\n  - OrderController reads order (found, ACTIVE)\n  - OrderController reads all shipments (finds S-1 CONFIRMED)\n  - Finds CONFIRMED shipment\n  - Throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 409 with error envelope\n  - Response: 409 with error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n  - Order and shipments in repository unchanged\n\n- **Non-existent order:**\n  - Request: POST /orders/O-99/cancel\n  - OrderController reads order (not found)\n  - Throws ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n  - Response: 404 with error code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n- **Create shipment for cancelled order:**\n  - Request: POST /shipments with orderId=O-1 (O-1 is CANCELLED)\n  - ShipmentController checks shipment doesn't exist (passes)\n  - OrderController checks order exists (found)\n  - Checks order is not CANCELLED (fails)\n  - Throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED\n  - Response: 409 with error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_transitions_shipments` - POST /orders/O-1/cancel where O-1 is ACTIVE with CREATED shipments, verify 200, order is CANCELLED, shipments are CANCELLED\n\n2. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotent` - POST /orders/O-1/cancel twice, both return 200\n\n3. `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_fails_409` - POST /orders/O-1/cancel where O-1 has CONFIRMED shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code, order and shipments unchanged\n\n4. `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - POST /orders/O-99/cancel, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\n5. `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_fails_409` - Cancel order O-1, then POST /shipments for O-1, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n6. `get_order_reports_status` - Create order, verify it has ACTIVE status; cancel it, verify it has CANCELLED status\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. Starting with the Order entity:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":24343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383ea776-af05-4287-8ce9-e006c6a2c176","uuid":"d84a1a01-ef24-4728-af0d-57e314c1ad90","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:43:10.205Z","request_id":"req_011CevL614vDnouH3T8EgvKp"}
