 Unknown order: `cancel nonexistent order returns 404` - returns NOT_FOUND\n   - Cancelled order rejects shipment: `rejects shipment creation for cancelled order with 409` - returns ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n6. **No new Maven dependency** ✓\n   - pom.xml unchanged (verified by scope - no new build file modifications)\n\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓\n   - Only modified files: Order.kt, OrderRepository.kt (actually not needed - see below), OrderController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ApiError.kt\n   - All modifications are directly related to cancel order feature\n\n**Diff Review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added status field (OrderStatus enum) to model the lifecycle\n   - Correctly defaults to ACTIVE for new orders\n   - Properly using enum for type safety\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added ORDER_CANCELLED to ErrorCode enum\n   - Needed for shipment rejection case when order is cancelled\n   - Follows existing enum pattern\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>\n   - Required to find all shipments for an order during cancellation\n   - Correctly filters and sorts by shipmentId\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added cancel endpoint with full logic\n   - Injected ShipmentRepository dependency\n   - Implements all requirements: idempotent, all-or-nothing, error handling\n   - Correctly uses repository methods for persistence\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added order status validation before shipment creation\n   - Injected OrderRepository dependency\n   - Checks order exists and is not CANCELLED\n   - Throws appropriate ConflictException for cancelled orders\n   - Preserves original behavior for orders that don't exist (allows shipment creation)\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added 6 comprehensive tests\n   - Tests cover all acceptance criteria cases\n   - Uses proper MockMvc assertions on both status and error body\n   - Tests include status field check on creation\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - MUST CHANGE: Added 1 test for shipment rejection\n   - Tests cannot create shipment for cancelled order\n   - Verifies error code and message\n   - Properly initializes order repository with cancelled order\n\n**Unresolved Findings:** None\n\nAll acceptance criteria are met. All existing tests pass. All new tests pass. Implementation follows existing patterns and conventions.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Implement POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing customers to cancel active orders, moving them to CANCELLED status and cancelling associated CREATED shipments, with idempotent behavior for already-cancelled orders, all-or-nothing rejection if any shipment is CONFIRMED, 404 for non-existent orders, and preventing shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       \n- Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class\n- ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED error code to ErrorCode enum\n- OrderController.kt — added cancel(@PathVariable orderId) endpoint with all-or-nothing logic and shipment cancellation\n- ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId(orderId) method to locate shipments for cancellation\n- ShipmentController.kt — added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — added 6 tests: status on creation, cancel success, shipment cancellation, idempotence, confirmed shipment blocks, non-existent order rejection\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests        \n- newly created order has ACTIVE status — verifies order status field defaults correctly\n- cancels an active order and returns 200 — verifies cancel endpoint returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n- cancel endpoint cancels CREATED shipments — verifies CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED during order cancellation\n- cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds idempotent — verifies second cancel returns 200 without change\n- cancel fails with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED — verifies all-or-nothing rejection with error code, order and shipments unchanged\n- cancel nonexistent order returns 404 — verifies ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n- rejects shipment creation for cancelled order with 409 — verifies ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nVerification  \nCommand: `./mvnw test`\nResult: BUILD SUCCESS with 20 tests (10 OrderControllerTest, 6 ShipmentControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 3 CustomerControllerTest), all passing with 0 failures\n\nNot done      Nothing"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":41433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":846},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383ea776-af05-4287-8ce9-e006c6a2c176","uuid":"7f9c070a-07be-44e0-a091-6fd07bf2b562","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:44:49.464Z","request_id":"req_011CevLDwWq2N5B7HRAarZJv"}
